= News

This page highlights current research directions, academic activities, and updates. It will be expanded as new results and presentations become publicly available.

== November 2026

*Ongoing — Detector response and reconstruction efficiency*

Continuing research on detector-response characterization and reconstruction efficiency for the XENONnT experiment. Current topics include energy-scale calibration, analysis-cut efficiency, and the diagnosis of event-reconstruction losses.

== Research Updates

- *XENONnT Science Run 2:* Detector gains, electron response, and energy-resolution studies.
- *Solar pp neutrino analysis:* Simulation-based efficiency studies using detector waveforms and realistic backgrounds.
- *Computational statistical physics:* Sampling and finite-size studies of the two-dimensional Potts model.

== Future Updates

Publications, posters, talks, and project milestones will be listed here once the relevant information is publicly available.
